After Effects Studio: local native AE control with a detailed production-derived motion language for any brand or style. Before designing or building motion, read ae_library documents motion-language, production-workflow and brief-template; load construction, camera-continuity, assets-depth, type-evidence and worked-scenes as relevant. This craft foundation is the default for ALL styles, not an optional JoeB preset. Everything required is bundled; do not require the original repo, personal rig or assets. Inspect ae_context and discover exact operations with ae_catalog. eval.run enables custom ES3. A batch is not transactional; inspect failures or uncertain completion before retrying. Render and visually inspect actual artifacts, and distinguish technical success from visual quality. The paper/navy/vermilion JoeB appearance is optional.

Discover available atomic operations for ae_do. Without args: all categories with their operation names. With a category: detailed params per operation. Only operations this server will actually execute are listed. This tool is part of plugin `After Effects Studio`.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__after_effects_studio__ae_catalog(args: {
  // Filter by category. Omit to list all categories with operation counts, then drill into a specific category.
  category?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

